<title>SOUTH KOREA: Asia Motors goes limit-up on sale news.</title>
<headline>Asia Motors goes limit-up on sale news.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in troubled Asia Motors hit their upper daily limit at Thursday's opening on news that Kia Group was considering selling the commercial vehicle maker, brokers said.  </p>
<p>Asia Motors rose 280 won, or 7.98 percent, to 3,790 at 0040 GMT.</p>
<p>However, a Kia Group spokesman said it was undecided when the final sale decision would be made by the group.</p>
<p>But a source close to Kia Group said a decision to sell was &quot;inevitable&quot; because of pressure by creditor banks.</p>
<p>&quot;The news helped attract buying interest,&quot; said a LG Securities broker.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5647</p>
</text>
